/home/epentland/ai/canopy/guardian-zig/FEEDBACK.md:9803:- **friction:** Another agent was editing two other files in the SAME worktree concurrently. Every filtered run of mine reported `run-all: 6/79 failed (spec, pub-api-surface, anytype-budget, dead-pub, orphan-files, test-reachability)` — all six from THEIR new `src/placement/manhattan_route.zig`, none from my file. Guardian's grouped output made attribution easy (each finding names its file), but there is no way to ask "show me only findings in the files I touched". A `--only-paths <glob>` (or "findings in files changed since <ref> BY me") would let a parallel agent read its own verdict without manually diffing the failure list against `git status`. Cost here was low (~2 minutes of reading), but it also means a real finding of mine could hide inside a wall of someone else's.
