/home/epentland/ai/canopy/guardian-zig/FEEDBACK.md:9845:- **friction (not Guardian's fault, but Guardian-adjacent):** the expensive part of this wave was diagnosing why copper my code demonstrably emitted did not appear in the routed output — a later pass was rewriting it. With no way to run one test, each hypothesis cost a full `zig build test-affected` (~2-3 min), and I spent six of them bisecting by hand with `log.progress` lines. Repeating last session's wish with a sharper edge: a `--guardian-filter` that actually narrows an ALREADY-BUILT shard binary (today the runtime flag is additive to the compiled filter set, so passing my own test name still ran all 656) would have turned each of those six iterations into seconds.
