/home/epentland/ai/canopy/guardian-zig/FEEDBACK.md:10189:## 2026-08-24 · codex · eda — recover PCB autosave failures
/home/epentland/ai/canopy/guardian-zig/FEEDBACK.md:10191:- **friction:** Guardian source changed repeatedly during verification while its installed checker remained stale. The documented `GUARDIAN_PREBUILT=off` override reused Zig's configure-time choice until paired with a fresh `ZIG_LOCAL_CACHE_DIR`; one attempt then compiled an intermediate dirty Guardian revision that no longer matched by completion. Cost: four failed/restarted build invocations and roughly four minutes before the EDA gate could run against a consistent checker.
/home/epentland/ai/canopy/guardian-zig/FEEDBACK.md:10193:## 2026-08-24 · codex · eda — merge undersized solder-mask webs
/home/epentland/ai/canopy/guardian-zig/FEEDBACK.md:10195:- **friction:** Guardian source was being edited concurrently while the installed checker stayed stale; `GUARDIAN_PREBUILT=off` only became reliable with a fresh local Zig cache, costing several failed verification attempts. Passing focused tests also printed `failed command:` after `guardian/test: PASS`, making the shell exit code the only unambiguous result.
/home/epentland/ai/canopy/guardian-zig/FEEDBACK.md:10197:## 2026-08-24 · codex · guardian-zig — resolve high-value usage feedback
/home/epentland/ai/canopy/guardian-zig/FEEDBACK.md:10198:- **good:** The focused regression set and two complete `zig build test` runs passed all 1,186 main tests, the runner's separate tests, and all 79 Guardian checks; the new build-level finalizer printed `guardian/test: PASS — complete build step succeeded` only after every sibling dependency completed, making the final result unambiguous despite Zig Maker's earlier `failed command:` warning.
/home/epentland/ai/canopy/guardian-zig/FEEDBACK.md:10200:- **friction:** Returning normally instead of `_exit(0)` from the server runner did not clear Zig Maker's misleading `failed command:` label; Maker classifies any successful server-mode stderr diagnostics as a warning. Resolving it without losing Guardian's counts, timings, and machine result required a top-level build finalizer with inherited stdio.
/home/epentland/ai/canopy/guardian-zig/FEEDBACK.md:10202:## 2026-08-24 · codex · eda — centre off-grid subcircuit GND vias
/home/epentland/ai/canopy/guardian-zig/FEEDBACK.md:10204:- **friction:** The first focused run could not reach the gate because the installed Guardian checker was stale against concurrently edited Guardian source, and `GUARDIAN_PREBUILT=off` still reused the stale configured helper. A manual `zig build` in Guardian was required before EDA verification could proceed, costing two failed focused invocations.
/home/epentland/ai/canopy/guardian-zig/FEEDBACK.md:10206:## 2026-08-24 · codex · eda — lock and unlock multi-selected components
/home/epentland/ai/canopy/guardian-zig/FEEDBACK.md:10209:## 2026-08-24 · codex · eda — show details for design-note update failures
/home/epentland/ai/canopy/guardian-zig/FEEDBACK.md:10211:- **friction:** The check's fix said to “alias once at file scope,” so the first correction used `const log = std.log.scoped(...)`; Guardian rejected that alias too, requiring a second gate run and a direct function alias (`const logError = std.log.err`). Naming that exact allowed form in the diagnostic would avoid the retry.
