/home/epentland/ai/canopy/guardian-zig/FEEDBACK.md:10931:## 2026-08-29 · claude-opus · guardian-zig — new check concurrency-test-presence
/home/epentland/ai/canopy/guardian-zig/FEEDBACK.md:10933:- **good:** Guardian's own rules made the check *better*. My first predicate was "a spawn inside a `test { }` body". Dogfooding it against the consumer showed that would be a FALSE POSITIVE on the best concurrency test in that tree, whose author had hoisted the spawn into a helper with the comment "Hoisted out of the test body: … `test-no-conditional` allows one [loop]". `test-no-conditional` *forces* the helper pattern, so a brace-position rule would have fought the rest of the suite. The shipped predicate credits a spawn a test reaches through the file-local call graph instead.
