/home/epentland/ai/canopy/guardian-zig/FEEDBACK.md:11169:- **friction:** The brief said "the baseline row disappears on the next whole-tree, write-allowed Guardian run", and a whole-tree `guardian-check all . --gate` is whole-tree but NOT write-allowed — it reported green and left the resolved row in the file, silently. The prune needed `zig build guardian-accept -Dguardian-checks=projection-completeness`. `baseline.zig`'s `reportOutcome` already has the right wording for this (`ok: <check>: N resolved (run guardian-check accept <check> . to prune the baseline)`), but on a 72-check run with 0 blocking findings that line is not printed at the verdict — the whole run collapses to `run-all: 72 checks — 0 blocking, 2 report-only`. Cost: one confused round trip diffing `.guardian/` and reading `baseline.zig` to find out why a resolved row survived a green whole-tree gate.
