/home/epentland/ai/canopy/guardian-zig/FEEDBACK.md:11324:## 2026-09-03 · claude · guardian-zig — fix three Guardian Arena defects
/home/epentland/ai/canopy/guardian-zig/FEEDBACK.md:11325:- **bug:** The stale-binary notice contradicted a passing selfcheck. The green stamp recorded the executable's CONTENT fingerprint, so two dep roots that each built the same Guardian source (byte-different links) read as different guardians; the direction then compared the running binary's mtime against the STAMP FILE's mtime — the moment the last gate ran, not when its binary was built — so a freshly built binary was reliably told it was "OLDER than the one that last gated the tree". Six eda worktrees hit it on green gates. The stamp now records the source digest `selfcheck` verifies (line 3) plus the gating binary's own mtime (line 4); a matching source digest can no longer produce the notice, and the direction is binary-mtime against binary-mtime.
/home/epentland/ai/canopy/guardian-zig/FEEDBACK.md:11328:- **good:** Guardian's own gate caught three real gaps in this patch that review had missed — `oom-discipline` on a new `allocPrint ... catch return false` that conflated OOM with "not wired", `repeated-string-literal` on a `"test-compile"` constant duplicated between build_helper and commit, and `test-coverage` on two new pub fns no test named.
/home/epentland/ai/canopy/guardian-zig/FEEDBACK.md:11330:## 2026-09-03 · codex · eda — repair adaptive PCB trace widths from authoritative DRC
