/home/epentland/ai/canopy/guardian-zig/FEEDBACK.md:11481:- **good:** The test runner's zero-match filter guard earned its keep on the first try. A new file's tests do not compile into Guardian's binary until `src/check.zig` lists `_ = @import(...)`, and I forgot; `zig build test -Dtest-filter=withScratch` printed `2 test(s) selected — 0 match by name, 2 unnamed test block(s) run regardless` and FAILED instead of exiting green. That is exactly the byte-identical-to-a-green-run trap it exists to close — without it I would have believed a new test passed on its first run.
