/home/epentland/ai/canopy/guardian-zig/FEEDBACK.md:11512:- **friction:** Adding a new test-bearing `.zig` file to eda needs three edits — the file, `src/test_root.zig`'s import bridge, and `src/test_shards.zig`'s filter list — and Guardian's own checks name none of them; the failure surfaced later as two failing tests in `test_root.zig` (`shard manifest runs every named test exactly once`, `the shard import bridge lists every module whose tests run`). Those tests are eda's, not Guardian's, and they did their job. But a project-side convention this mechanical is the shape a Guardian check catches cheaply: a new `src/**.zig` containing `test "` whose module is absent from a configured registry file. Compare `spec`'s unlinked-tag hint, which hands you the exact bullet to paste — here I had to read two test bodies to work out what they wanted.
